sentences.l:
and the earth groaned beneath, as under Zeus delighting-in-the-thunderbolt
incensed, when about Typhoeus he lashes the earth
among the Arimi, where they say are the beds of Typhoeus;

who beyond all others
knew seercraft, and nor his own sons did he keep allowing
to go to man-wasting war;

But Pyraechmes brought the Paeonians of the curved bows
from far away, from Amydon, from the Axius flowing wide,
the Axius whose fairest water spreads over the earth.

Nastes, in turn, led the Carians of barbarian speech,
who held Miletus and the mountain of the Phthires, of unsorted leaves,
and the streams of the Maeander and the steep peaks of Mycale;
